`startingNodes` is iterated twice in quick succession — once to build the initial `queue` array via `Array.from(startingNodes, ...)` (line 20) and again with `startingNodes.forEach(...)` to populate `visited` (lines 23–25). These can be combined into a single pass:
```ts
const queue: { node: ModuleNode; distance: number }[] = [];
startingNodes.forEach((node) => {
  visited.set(node, 0);
  queue.push({ node, distance: 0 });
});
```
